{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "clojure",
  "name": "Clojure (JVM backend)",
  "versions": {
    "stable": "1.12.6",
    "as_of": "2026-11"
  },
  "detect": [
    {
      "file": "deps.edn"
    },
    {
      "file": "project.clj"
    },
    {
      "file": "workspace.edn"
    }
  ],
  "scope": {
    "pkgs": [
      "src",
      "test"
    ],
    "pkg_dirs": [
      "src",
      "test"
    ]
  },
  "source_globs": [
    "**/*.clj",
    "**/*.cljc"
  ],
  "test_globs": [
    "test/**/*_test.clj",
    "test/**/*_test.cljc",
    "**/test/**/*_test.clj",
    "**/test/**/*_test.cljc"
  ],
  "generated": {
    "globs": [
      "**/target/**",
      "**/classes/**"
    ]
  },
  "manifest": "deps.edn",
  "variants": [
    {
      "name": "lein",
      "detect": [
        {
          "file": "project.clj"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "name": "deps",
          "argv": [
            "lein",
            "deps"
          ],
          "when_file": [
            "project.clj"
          ],
          "tool": "lein"
        },
        {
          "name": "cljfmt",
          "argv": [
            "lein",
            "cljfmt",
            "check"
          ],
          "tool": "lein-cljfmt",
          "install": "add [dev.weavejester/lein-cljfmt \"0.16.6\"] to :plugins in project.clj"
        },
        {
          "name": "test",
          "argv": [
            "lein",
            "cloverage",
            "--lcov",
            "--no-html",
            "--output",
            "{coverage_dir}"
          ],
          "tool": "lein-cloverage",
          "note": "Leiningen variant: project.clj needs the lein-cloverage plugin (D13)"
        },
        {
          "name": "test-repeat",
          "argv": [
            "lein",
            "kaocha",
            "--randomize",
            "--seed",
            "{seed}"
          ],
          "tool": "lein",
          "note": "Leiningen variant: needs a kaocha alias in project.clj (D13)"
        }
      ],
      "test_commands": [
        {
          "argv_prefix": [
            "lein",
            "test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "argv_prefix": [
            "lein",
            "kaocha"
          ]
        },
        {
          "argv_prefix": [
            "lein",
            "cloverage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "argv_prefix": [
            "bin/kaocha"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "name": "deps",
      "kind": "deps",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-P",
        "-M:test"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "tool": "clojure",
      "when_file": [
        "deps.edn"
      ],
      "note": "prefetch only: resolves and downloads, never edits deps.edn (D11)"
    },
    {
      "name": "cljfmt",
      "kind": "format",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-Tcljfmt",
        "check"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "tool": "cljfmt",
      "when_file": [
        ".cljfmt.edn",
        "cljfmt.edn"
      ],
      "install": "clojure -Ttools install-latest :lib io.github.weavejester/cljfmt :as cljfmt",
      "note": "required only when the project committed a cljfmt config (D14)"
    },
    {
      "name": "clj-kondo",
      "kind": "lint",
      "argv": [
        "clj-kondo",
        "--lint",
        "{pkgs}",
        "--parallel"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "tool": "clj-kondo",
      "exit_codes": {
        "0": "pass",
        "2": "fail",
        "3": "fail"
      },
      "install": "brew install borkdude/brew/clj-kondo",
      "note": "exit 2 = warnings, 3 = errors (default --fail-level warning); for a Polylith workspace pass --pkgs components bases projects"
    },
    {
      "name": "poly",
      "kind": "arch",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:poly",
        "check"
      ],
      "required": false,
      "tool": "poly",
      "when_file": [
        "workspace.edn"
      ],
      "note": "Polylith interface and dependency rules; the :poly alias is part of the Polylith workspace"
    },
    {
      "name": "arch",
      "kind": "arch",
      "internal": "arch",
      "required": false
    },
    {
      "name": "test",
      "kind": "test",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:cov",
        "-o",
        "{coverage_dir}"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "tool": "clojure",
      "signal_regex": "FAIL in|ERROR in|Execution error|Syntax error|Uncaught exception|Failed \\d+ of|Ran \\d+ tests",
      "note": "cloverage runs clojure.test, not Kaocha; the :cov alias is a D13 prerequisite"
    },
    {
      "name": "test-repeat",
      "kind": "test",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:test",
        "--randomize",
        "--seed",
        "{seed}"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "tool": "clojure",
      "repeat": 3,
      "signal_regex": "FAIL in|ERROR in|Execution error|failures?[,.]|Randomized with --seed",
      "note": "race substitute: Kaocha randomised order, 3 runs with different printed seeds; tests.edn and the :test alias are D13 prerequisites"
    },
    {
      "name": "coverage",
      "kind": "coverage",
      "internal": "coverage",
      "required": true,
      "skippable": false
    },
    {
      "name": "nvd",
      "kind": "vuln",
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-J-Dclojure.main.report=stderr",
        "-Tnvd",
        "nvd.task/check",
        ":classpath",
        "\"{classpath}\"",
        ":config-filename",
        "\"nvd-clojure.edn\""
      ],
      "required": false,
      "tool": "nvd-clojure",
      "default": "off",
      "env_required": [
        "NVD_API_TOKEN"
      ],
      "install": "clojure -Ttools install nvd-clojure/nvd-clojure '{:mvn/version \"RELEASE\"}' :as nvd",
      "note": "needs an NVD API key; the EDN strings are quoted on purpose (-T parses them)"
    }
  ],
  "security": {"checks": ["nvd"]},
  "test_commands": [
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:cov"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "clojure",
        "-X:test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "clojure",
        "-M:kaocha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "bin/kaocha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "lein",
        "test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "argv_prefix": [
        "lein",
        "kaocha"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "race": {
    "mode": "none",
    "checks": [
      "test-repeat"
    ],
    "reason": "The JVM and Clojure have no general data-race detector; immutable data and managed references (atom, ref, agent) remove most races by construction",
    "substitute": "the test-repeat check: Kaocha randomised order, 3 runs with different printed seeds (--randomize --seed N); concurrency-tagged tests repeated 20 times (--focus-meta :concurrency) and reflection warnings clean stay review items (CLJ-CONC-08)"
  },
  "coverage": {
    "format": "lcov",
    "path": "{coverage_dir}/lcov.info",
    "produced_by": [
      "test"
    ],
    "granularity": "form",
    "exclude": [
      "test/**",
      "**/test/**",
      "dev/**",
      "development/**",
      "**/target/**",
      "build.clj"
    ],
    "source_roots": [
      "src"
    ]
  },
  "placeholders": {
    "classpath": {
      "argv": [
        "clojure",
        "-Spath",
        "-M:test"
      ]
    }
  },
  "post_edit": {
    "format_file": [
      "cljfmt",
      "fix",
      "{file}"
    ],
    "lint_dir": [
      "clj-kondo",
      "--lint",
      "{dir}"
    ]
  },
  "cache_env": {
    "JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS": "-Djava.io.tmpdir={tmp}"
  },
  "shared_env": [
    "GITLIBS",
    "CLJ_CONFIG"
  ],
  "artifacts": [
    "target/",
    ".cpcache/",
    ".clj-kondo/.cache/",
    ".lsp/.cache/",
    ".nrepl-port",
    "classes/",
    "*.class",
    "*.hprof",
    "hs_err_pid*.log",
    ".lein-failures",
    ".lein-repl-history",
    "**/target/",
    ".metrics/"
  ],
  "arch": {
    "parser": "regex",
    "import_regex": "\\[\\s*([a-z][A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]*(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]+)+)(?:\\s|\\])",
    "resolver": "dotted-module-underscore",
    "native_check": "poly",
    "forbidden_in_domain": [
      "clojure.java.io",
      "clojure.java.shell",
      "clojure.java.jdbc",
      "next.jdbc",
      "honey.sql",
      "ring.",
      "reitit.",
      "org.httpkit",
      "clj-http",
      "hato",
      "clojure.core.async"
    ],
    "impure_calls": [
      "System/currentTimeMillis",
      "Instant/now",
      "LocalDate/now",
      "(rand",
      "random-uuid",
      "UUID/randomUUID",
      "(slurp",
      "(spit",
      "(future",
      "(swap!",
      "(reset!"
    ]
  },
  "config_files": [
    ".clj-kondo/config.edn",
    ".cljfmt.edn",
    "cljfmt.edn",
    "tests.edn",
    ".editorconfig",
    ".lsp/config.edn",
    "deps.edn",
    "project.clj",
    "workspace.edn",
    "nvd-clojure.edn",
    ".tool-versions"
  ],
  "sources": {
    "checks": "https://clojure.org/reference/clojure_cli",
    "deps": "https://clojure.org/reference/deps_edn",
    "cljfmt": "https://github.com/weavejester/cljfmt",
    "clj-kondo": "https://github.com/clj-kondo/clj-kondo#readme",
    "coverage": "https://github.com/cloverage/cloverage",
    "kaocha": "https://github.com/lambdaisland/kaocha",
    "vuln": "https://github.com/rm-hull/nvd-clojure",
    "race": "https://clojure.org/reference/atoms",
    "polylith": "https://cljdoc.org/d/polylith/clj-poly/CURRENT/doc/readme",
    "leiningen": "https://leiningen.org/"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Project rules win: use the project's own aliases, tests.edn and kondo/cljfmt config; log overrides with loops run override.",
    "D13 prerequisites (architect or clojure-engineer, wave 0): a :test alias running Kaocha (tests.edn, #kaocha/v1) and a :cov alias running cloverage with main-opts [\"-m\" \"cloverage.coverage\" \"-p\" \"src\" \"-s\" \"test\" \"--lcov\" \"--no-html\"]; loops appends -o {coverage_dir}. The snippet is in skills/lang-clojure/testing.md.",
    "cloverage writes lcov.info with relative SF: paths (src/...).",
    "Caches (D15): ~/.m2 and ~/.gitlibs are shared; CLJ_CACHE has no effect with a project deps.edn, so ./.cpcache is cleaned (artifacts) instead of redirected.",
    "A project with both deps.edn and project.clj gets the lein variant; pin the variant in .loops/config.json languages, or drop the unused manifest (CLJ-REPO-03).",
    "arch: the regex scanner reads dotted namespaces in [..] vectors of ns forms; single-segment namespaces and prefix lists ([a.b [c] [d]]) are not resolved, so Polylith workspaces also run poly check."
  ]
}
